# ── Site records. Never commit these ──────────────────────────────────
#
# They hold the customer's IPs, MACs, device list and switch names verbatim.
# Once pushed, deleting them does not take them out of the commit history.
scan-history.json
port-history.json
isolation.json

# The names used up to v3.0. The program migrates them to the new names on
# start, but they are listed here too in case a commit happens first.
스캔기록.json
포트기록.json
격리기록.json
기준선.json

# The device book as edited on site.
#
# The shipped book (device-book.json) belongs in the repository — without it the
# program cannot name vendors. Additions go to this file instead, so the shipped
# one is never dirtied.
device-book.local.json
장비사전.내것.json
*.json.tmp

# Exported documents. Site material.
*.xlsx
*.csv
준공리포트*
현장리포트*
report_*
세션*.json

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/
dist/
IPFixBackend/
electron/dist/
electron/installer/
electron/node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
build.log

# ── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Leftovers and scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The leading / limits this to the repository root. Written as a bare name it
# would also match electron/renderer/IPFixStudio.ico and the app icon disappears.
/IPFixStudio.ico
_old_*
_paths_test.py
